  "notes": [
   "Steps are pictures only; exact stud-level positions are inferred, so most ports are left null.",
   "Main body: wedge b1 with two 2x2 groove tiles and two 1x3 tiles on top. The two 63868 clip plates sit on its underside, each carrying a round boat-stud plate (b8, b9).",
   "The third round plate b10 with the blue 1x2 plate b11, the side-handle plate b12 and the two trans-blue 1x1 studs is a sub-assembly. It is assumed to attach to the wedge through b11.",
   "Cockpit sub-assembly: slope b16 and curved brick b17 on plate b15. Arm b18 clips onto b15's handle and onto the clip of 63868 b6.",
   "Wing sub-assembly (2x): the 48336 handle plate is clipped into the 60470a clips plate. Each wing's 60470a free clip is assumed to grip the bar of the 2540 plate b12, which has a bar at each end. The exact arrangement of curved bricks, blue plates and grille tiles within a wing is a best reading of the pictures.",
   "The 48336 and 60470a clip joins use clip.1 to clip.1, which is an assumption."
  ]
 },
